<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Hindmarsh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1785">1785</a>–<a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir John Hindmarsh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir John Hindmarsh was a British naval officer who fought at the battles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and Trafalgar and became the first governor of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. He proclaimed the province at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holdfast-bay">Holdfast Bay</a> in December 1836 but quarrelled with the resident commissioner and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-light">William Light</a> over the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide">Adelaide</a>, and was recalled in 1838. He later served as lieutenant governor of Heligoland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-hindmarsh.jpg" alt="John Hindmarsh" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Hindmarsh_2.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
